The Technical RequirementsTo show tray icons, your Python script must do three things on the D-Bus session bus:

Register ownership of the org.freedesktop.StatusNotifierWatcher name.
Listen for the RegisterStatusNotifierItem method call from applications.
Fetch the IconName or IconPixmap from the registered app path and render it in GTK.


Before connecting, you need to understand the four addressing elements of a D-Bus target:

Bus Type: Usually the System Bus (for hardware and system events) or Session Bus (per user login, for desktop apps).
Service Name: A reverse-domain string identifying the app (e.g., org.freedesktop.UPower).
Object Path: A filesystem-like path pointing to a specific object inside the app (e.g., /org/freedesktop/UPower/devices/DisplayDevice).
Interface & Method: The specific namespace and function you want to trigger (e.g., Interface org.freedesktop.UPower.Device calling the Get method).